d:110:  - 角落的 magenta 标记像素在输出中保持不变。所有对象保持不变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:111:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:112:- `Key insight`：本题有两层非显然推理：（1）连线路径并非自由选择的最短路径，而是固定采用\"先水平后垂直\"的 L 形策略——需要观察所有拐弯点都出现在同一对的水平对齐位置来归纳；（2）连线颜色并非始终是对象颜色——直线连接保留原色，L 形连接变为 magenta。角落的 magenta 标记看似装饰，实则定义了 L 形路径的替代颜色，需要跨样例比较才能发现它的作用。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:113:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:114:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:115:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:116:- `description`：在由围墙分隔成若干房间的网格中，围墙缺口（门）将房间串联成一条链；从标记房间开始沿链依次为每个房间填充固定色序中的下一种颜色。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:117:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:118:- `Input structure`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:119:  - 背景为 black。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:120:  - 网格中有 green 围墙像素（1 像素厚），将网格分割为若干封闭的\"房间\"（房间内部为 black）。房间形状为不规则多边形，大小各异。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:121:  - 每两个相邻房间之间的共享墙段上最多有一个\"门\"——即围墙上一个单像素的 black 缺口，使得两个房间通过该缺口 4-连通。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:122:  - 所有房间通过门形成一条不分叉的链（即存在一种遍历方式，从某个端点房间出发，经过门依次到达每个房间恰好一次，不回头）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:123:  - 链的一个端点房间（即只与一个门相邻的房间）内包含一个 red 标记像素。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:124:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:125:- `Rule`：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:126:  - 从包含 red 标记的端点房间开始，沿着门的连接关系依次遍历所有房间。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:127:  - 按遍历顺序为每个房间分配颜色，使用固定色序循环：第 1 个房间为 red，第 2 个为 orange，第 3 个为 yellow，第 4 个为 blue，第 5 个为 magenta，第 6 个为 azure。若房间数超过 6 个，从 red 重新开始循环。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:128:  - 用分配的颜色填充每个房间的全部内部 black 像素（包括覆盖原 red 标记像素）。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:129:  - 围墙保持 green 不变，门（black 缺口）保持 black 不变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:130:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:131:- `Key insight`：本题有三层推理：（1）识别围墙上的单像素缺口是\"门\"，门连接相邻房间——需要理解空间拓扑连通性；（2）发现所有房间通过门形成一条线性链，且链的起点由 red 标记指定——需要从标记房间出发追踪门的连接关系确定遍历顺序；（3）房间的填充颜色按固定色序 red→orange→yellow→blue→magenta→azure 循环分配——需要从样例中归纳出这一特定色序而非其他可能的排列。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/des.md:132:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:1:你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:3:每个参考题描述包含：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:4:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:5:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:6:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:7:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:9:参考题目如下：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:10:<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"7ec998c9\" lines=\"14-28\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:11:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:12:Draw a blue folded corner-to-corner route through the lone marker's column.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:13:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:14:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:15:- A rectangular grid filled with one background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:16:- Exactly one non-background marker pixel; blue is absent from the input.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:17:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:18:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:19:- Preserve the marker and repaint background pixels in its column blue from top to bottom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:20:- If the marker is in the unique center column, connect that column to the top-right and bottom-left corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:21:- Otherwise, connect the column to the top-left and bottom-right corners.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:22:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:23:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:24:The marker's column is the route spine; its central vs off-center placement selects which opposite corner pair gets the horizontal edge segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:25:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:26:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:27:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:28:<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"2ba387bc\" lines=\"6-21\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:29:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:30:Sort scattered 4×4 squares into two columns by type: frames left, solids right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:31:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:32:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:33:- bg = most common color. Multiple 4×4 objects on bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:34:- Frames: colored 1px border, bg-filled 2×2 interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:35:- Solids: entirely filled with one non-bg color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:36:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:37:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:38:- Classify each 4×4 object as frame or solid by its interior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:39:- Sort each group top-to-bottom by input row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:40:- Stack frames in left column (cols 0–3), solids in right (cols 4–7).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:41:- Output is 8 wide; height = 4 × max(#frames, #solids), bg-padded.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:42:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:43:Key insight: Frame vs solid is determined solely by whether the 2×2 interior matches bg.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:44:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:45:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:46:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:47:<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"aaef0977\" lines=\"25-41\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:48:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:49:Replace an orange canvas with concentric Manhattan-distance color rings centered on the lone marker pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:50:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:51:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:52:- The grid is an orange background with exactly one non-orange marker pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:53:- The marker color is one of the colors in the fixed non-orange ring cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:54:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:55:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:56:- The marker location is distance 0 and keeps the marker color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:57:- Each step of Manhattan distance away from the marker advances one position\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:58:  through the cycle green, yellow, black, grey, red, teal, maroon, pink, blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:59:- Fill every pixel of the original grid by this distance-indexed cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:60:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:61:Key insight: The output is not copied from existing objects; it is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:62:distance field around the single marker, colored by a cyclic palette that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:63:excludes the orange background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:64:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:65:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:66:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:67:<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"271d71e2\" lines=\"9-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:68:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:69:Move bordered containers toward same-colored destination markers, charging gray cells to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:70:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:71:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:72:- bg = 6 (magenta). Black-bordered (0) rectangles with gray (5) / orange (7) interiors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:73:- A head sprite (9) sits adjacent to one container edge; a matching destination sprite lies along the movement axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:74:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:75:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:76:- Each container translates toward its destination along the head-to-dest axis.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:77:- Steps = min(head-to-dest distance, number of gray interior cells).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:78:- Gray cells become orange from the head-facing side inward, one per step.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:79:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:80:Key insight: Gray cell count caps movement — a container stops short if it runs out of gray cells to charge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:81:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:82:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:83:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:84:<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"c4d1a9ae\" lines=\"28-48\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:85:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:86:Fill each vertical foreground band's background cells with the color of the next band to its right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:87:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:88:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:89:- The dominant color is the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:90:- Each other color occupies a separate vertical band defined by that color's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:91:  minimum and maximum columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:92:- Within a band, all cells are either that band's color or background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:93:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:94:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:95:- Order the bands from left to right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:96:- In each band, replace background pixels with the color of the next band in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:97:  that order, wrapping from the rightmost band back to the leftmost.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:98:- Preserve all existing foreground pixels and all background pixels outside\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:99:  the bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:100:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:101:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:102:- The column bands form a cyclic palette legend: a band's gaps are completed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:103:  by borrowing the color from its right-hand neighbor, not by changing the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:104:  band's existing pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:105:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:106:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:107:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:108:<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b745798f\" lines=\"18-33\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:109:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:110:Expand each 3-pixel L marker into a same-color corner L on an empty background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:111:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:112:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:113:- The grid is an odd square with one dominant background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:114:- Every foreground object is a monochromatic 4-connected 3-pixel L inside a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:115:  2x2 box.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:116:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:117:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:118:- Clear the grid to the background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:119:- For each marker, map its L orientation to the corresponding outer corner\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:120:  and draw that corner L in the marker color with arm length half the grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:121:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:122:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:123:- The small marker is a miniature corner; its orientation, not its position,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:124:  chooses which outer corner receives the expanded L.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:125:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:126:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:127:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:128:<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"6ca952ad\" lines=\"15-30\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:129:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:130:Drop every large foreground object straight down to the bottom while leaving small marker objects fixed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:131:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:132:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:133:- The grid has a dominant background color and exactly one foreground color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:134:- The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:135:- Objects of area at most three are stationary markers; larger objects are moving sprites.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:136:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:137:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:138:- Clear each moving sprite from its original position.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:139:- Translate each moving sprite vertically downward until its bbox bottom reaches the grid bottom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:140:- Repaint each translated sprite in its original color; small markers stay unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:141:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:142:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:143:- Object area separates the active falling sprites from the small fixed markers, and all active sprites follow the same vertical path.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:144:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:145:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:146:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:147:<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b2bc3ffd\" lines=\"8-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:148:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:149:Move every object above the solid bottom stripe upward by its own pixel count.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:150:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:151:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:152:The grid has a dominant background, exactly one full-width non-background row\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:153:that acts as a fixed stripe, and one or more 4-connected monochrome objects\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:154:above that stripe.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:155:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:156:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:157:Clear each object from its original cells, then translate it straight upward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:158:by the number of pixels in that object, preserving its shape and color. Leave\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:159:the full-width stripe unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:160:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:161:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:162:Each object's area is also its vertical displacement; the full-width row is a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:163:fixed baseline, not a moving object.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:164:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:165:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:166:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:167:<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"e12f9a14\" lines=\"138-152\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:168:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:169:Emit diagonal beams from framed 2x2 blocks through frame gaps; beams interact on collision.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:170:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:171:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:172:- bg = most common color. Wall color (e.g. green) forms 4x4 frames around 2x2 monochrome blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:173:- Each frame has one or more gap pixels where the wall is missing.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:174:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:175:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:176:- Each gap emits a beam of the inner block's color, traveling diagonally outward (direction set by gap position relative to the block).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:177:- Beams paint every cell they cross until they hit the grid edge or collide.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:178:- 90° collision: both beams turn 45° toward their bisector direction; the intersection cell is left blank (1-pixel gap).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:179:- 45° collision: beams merge into a zigzag (alternating cardinal + diagonal steps) with no gap at the meeting point.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:180:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:181:Key insight: Two distinct collision rules — 90° produces a gap and single-pixel diagonal lines; 45° produces no gap and thicker zigzag bands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:182:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:183:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:184:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:185:<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"8a6d367c\" lines=\"52-67\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:186:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:187:Complete the framed area by expanding the unique upper template that contains the existing seed pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:188:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:189:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:190:- A teal background contains small colored template masks above a larger rectangular frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:191:- The frame encloses one fill color arranged as a partial block-scaled copy of one template.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:192:- The frame interior dimensions are an integer square scale of the matching template bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:193:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:194:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:195:- Crop to the rectangular frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:196:- Identify the unique upper template whose block-scaled mask covers every existing fill pixel inside the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:197:- Reset the frame interior to background and paint the whole scaled mask with the fill color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:198:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:199:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:200:The lower colored pixels are seed cells that reveal which upper template should be completed inside the frame.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:201:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:202:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:203:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:204:<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"2a28add5\" lines=\"8-22\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:205:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:206:Paint each pink control pixel as a teal horizontal bar whose reach equals the foreground counts on that row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:207:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:208:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:209:- The grid has a dominant background color and one or more pink control pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:210:- Each marker row has exactly one pink pixel; all other non-background pixels\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:211:  in that row are counters.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:212:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:213:- Start from an all-background output grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:214:- For each pink pixel, count non-background pixels strictly to its left and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:215:  strictly to its right in the same row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:216:- Paint teal from c - left_count through c + right_count on that row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:217:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:218:- The foreground pixels are not copied; only their counts on each side of\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:219:  each pink marker encode the teal bar length.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:220:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:221:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:222:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:223:<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3cd86f4f\" lines=\"6-18\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:224:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:225:Shear the rectangular input down-left onto a black canvas.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:226:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:227:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:228:A rectangular grid of colored pixels with no internal empty region to infer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:229:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:230:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:231:Create a black output with the same height and width W + H - 1, then copy\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:232:each input row r unchanged starting at column H - 1 - r.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:233:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:234:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:235:The colors and row contents are preserved; only the row offsets change so\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:236:the left edge forms a descending diagonal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:237:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:238:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:239:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:240:<reference_puzzle index=\"13\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"ecb67b6d\" lines=\"138-155\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:241:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:242:Recolor the grey diagonal-chain regions in an orange field to teal.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:243:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:244:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:245:The input contains only grey pixels and orange pixels.  Grey pixels form\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:246:several 8-connected regions embedded in the orange field.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:247:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:248:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:249:Decompose each grey 8-connected region into 4-connected lobes.  Recolor the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:250:whole region teal only when it contains a straight diagonal run of at least\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:251:three pixels and those lobes meet only by diagonal corner contacts in a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:252:non-branching diagonal chain or cycle; a single 4-connected region is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:253:recolored only when it is a square diagonal staircase.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:254:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:255:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:256:The teal regions are not selected by size or position; they are the grey\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:257:regions whose internal connectivity depends on diagonal corner joins, while\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:258:same-edge cracks, rectangles, bars, and branching/noisy regions remain grey.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:259:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:260:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:261:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:262:<reference_puzzle index=\"14\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3bd292e8\" lines=\"13-29\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:263:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:264:Recolor wall-separated background regions alternately, starting with grey in the lower-left region.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:265:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:266:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:267:- The grid has one dominant background color and one foreground wall color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:268:- The wall pixels form one or more 4-connected one-cell-thick segments.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:269:- Each wall segment separates exactly two 4-connected background regions.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:270:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:271:- Keep all wall pixels unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:272:- Label the 4-connected background regions and connect two labels when they\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:273:  touch opposite sides of the same wall segment.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:274:- Color the region containing the lower-left corner grey, then flip between\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:275:  grey and green across every wall adjacency.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:276:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:277:- The red walls define a bipartite map of regions; the lower-left background\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:278:  region fixes which side of the alternating coloring is grey.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:279:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:280:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:281:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:282:<reference_puzzle index=\"15\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"fc4aaf52\" lines=\"17-34\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:283:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:284:Split the two-color object horizontally, swap its colors, and slide the upper half to the right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:285:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:286:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:287:- The grid has one background color and exactly two foreground colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:288:- All foreground pixels form one 4-connected object with an even-height bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:289:- The object has foreground pixels on both rows adjacent to its horizontal midpoint.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:290:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:291:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:292:- Split the object into upper and lower halves at the midpoint of its bbox.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:293:- Swap the two foreground colors in both halves.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:294:- Keep the lower half in place and shift the upper half right until its lower-left\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:295:  boundary pixel is diagonally adjacent to the lower half's upper-right boundary pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:296:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:297:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:298:- The object is not copied or reflected; it is broken at the horizontal waist,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:299:  recolored by exchanging the two visible object colors, then rejoined diagonally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:300:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:301:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:302:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:303:<reference_puzzle index=\"16\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"80214e03\" lines=\"48-64\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:304:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:305:Extract the color of each noisy block in a row/column lattice and mirror the coarse grid horizontally.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:306:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:307:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:308:- A background surrounds a rectangular lattice of monochrome foreground blocks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:309:- Consecutive rows in a lattice band share the same set of visible foreground colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:310:- Consecutive columns in a lattice band share the same set of visible foreground colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:311:- Each row-band/column-band intersection has one foreground color, with possible background holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:312:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:313:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:314:- Group non-empty rows and columns into consecutive bands by their foreground color sets.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:315:- Replace each lattice cell by the single foreground color inside that row/column-band intersection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:316:- Return the resulting coarse color grid with the column order reversed.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:317:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:318:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:319:- Whole-row and whole-column color sets reveal the hidden lattice even when neighboring cells share a color or contain holes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:320:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:321:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:322:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:323:<reference_puzzle index=\"17\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"342dd610\" lines=\"18-36\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:324:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:325:Move every foreground pixel by the fixed offset indicated by its color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:326:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:327:Input structure:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:328:- The grid has a unique dominant background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:329:- The foreground is a sparse set of colored pixels.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:330:- Each foreground color is one of the trained motion colors: orange, red,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:331:  maroon, or blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:332:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:333:Rule:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:334:- Clear the canvas to the background color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:335:- Translate orange pixels up 2 cells, red pixels left 2 cells, maroon\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:336:  pixels down 2 cells, and blue pixels right 1 cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:337:- Preserve each moved pixel's original color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:338:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:339:Key insight:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:340:The foreground color is the motion instruction; position only determines\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:341:where that color-specific displacement lands.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:342:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:343:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:344:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:345:<reference_puzzle index=\"18\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"9b30e358\" lines=\"9-23\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:346:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:347:Repeat the bottom foreground motif upward until it fills the whole grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:348:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:349:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:350:- The background is the dominant color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:351:- The only foreground pixels occupy a contiguous block of rows at the bottom.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:352:- That bottom block is the complete vertical motif, including its background cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:353:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:354:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:355:- Copy the bottom motif rows repeatedly upward across the full grid.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:356:- Preserve horizontal alignment and vertical phase: the original first motif row remains at its input row.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:357:- The output shape is unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:358:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:359:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:360:The blank rows above the bottom foreground block are missing repetitions of the same row motif, not empty space.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:361:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:362:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:363:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:364:<reference_puzzle index=\"19\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"b25e450b\" lines=\"28-43\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:365:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:366:Slide each black border rectangle to the opposite border, recoloring its swept stripe orange and leaving the rectangle black at the far edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:367:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:368:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:369:- The grid contains black rectangular 4-connected masks, each touching exactly one outer border.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:370:- Grey cells form incidental pattern content; orange is the trail color used when a black mask slides.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:371:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:372:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:373:- Treat all black rectangles as moving simultaneously.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:374:- A rectangle touching the top or bottom edge moves vertically to the opposite edge in the same columns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:375:- A rectangle touching the left or right edge moves horizontally to the opposite edge in the same rows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:376:- Recolor the complete swept row or column stripe to orange, then stamp every destination rectangle in black.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:377:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:378:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:379:- Edge contact gives the slide direction; the output is the set of opposite-edge black rectangles plus their orange trails.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:380:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:381:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:382:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:383:<reference_puzzle index=\"20\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"42f14c03\" lines=\"75-83\">\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:384:<description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:385:Crop the foreground object whose missing cells match marker shapes, and fill those missing cells with the marker colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:386:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:387:Input structure\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:388:A dominant background surrounds several monochromatic foreground objects. Exactly one object has background gaps inside its bounding box whose component shapes are matched by separate marker objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:389:Rule\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:390:Find that object, crop its bounding box, and replace each background gap component with the color of the separate marker component or components having the same normalized shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:391:Key insight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:392:The marker objects do not mark absolute positions; their shapes identify which gaps in the selected object should be colored, while objects with unmatched gaps are distractors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:393:</description>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:394:</reference_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:395:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:396:你的任务：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:397:以参考题为标杆，运用发散性思维进行创新扩展。请发挥创造力，构思全新且巧妙的推理谜题。用中文创造全新的 ARC 谜题描述。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:398:创新方式包括但不限于：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:399:**机制重组**：将多道参考题各自的核心机制提取出来，组合成一个新的多步管道，用到新的场景。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:400:**机制变异**：取几道参考题的核心机制，以机制为基础进行创新并与其他多种机制进行创新重组，使解题路径发生质变而非量变。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:401:**逆向构造**：取一道参考题的输出模式，思考\"什么样的输入规则能产生类似的输出结构但需要完全不同的推理过程\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:402:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:403:严格使用下面的 XML 风格格式输出：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:404:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:405:<new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:406:- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:407:- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:408:- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:409:- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:410:</new_puzzle>\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:411:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:412:请一次性生成5个`<new_puzzle>`，若有较多合适的创新，也可以生成更多，不设上限，但不要输出额外解释。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:413:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:414:注意事项：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:415:1. 任务不应依赖大量先验知识或复杂计算，而应依赖对模式、结构与空间关系的直觉推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:416:2. 关于\"计算\"的边界：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:417:   - **允许使用**（这些都是人类能心算的视觉量）：数像素 / 孔洞 / 对象 / 邻居（≤10 量级）、比大小、按某个可见属性排序、奇偶判断、取最大 / 最小、用一个计数值作为另一个等量几何量（如 N 个像素 → 长度 N 的射线、面积 N → 边长 N）、判断接触 / 相邻 / 包含、粗略中心位置（簇的视觉中点）、\"距离\"作为\"几步\"而不是公式等人类能够直观感受计算的内容。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:418:   - **禁止使用**（这些是算法量而非视觉量，会迫使解题者依赖公式而非视觉直觉）：曼哈顿 / 欧氏 / Chebyshev 距离作为精确查表键、凸包面积、二进制位编码 / 位运算、模运算（取模） / 余数、拓扑距离（BFS / 最短路 / 跳数）、精确几何质心坐标、凸角 / 凹角计数等复杂且不易被看出来的计算都是禁止使用的。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:419:3. 问题必须能从少量示例中推断出来（通常为 3 对训练样例 + 1 个测试样例）。设计时从人类解题者的视觉角度思考：规则涉及的所有关键要素（对象、关系、属性）必须在网格上肉眼可见，不应依赖人眼无法直接观察到的隐含信息（例如颜色id和颜色亮度是禁止使用的）或需要推算的隐藏属性。规则背后的逻辑本身可以有一定挑战性，但解题所需的所有线索必须能从网格中直接获取。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:420:4. 生成的问题描述旨在促进后续用于创建题目网格的代码生成。因此，对输入 / 输出网格的描述以及规则总结必须极其详细；语言风格应易于理解；对于特定对象（如箭头），必须在描述中明确其绘制方式。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:421:5. 描述谜题时避免使用 0 或 1 这类颜色编号；应使用颜色名称，例如 \"red\"。可用颜色如下：Black、Blue、Red、Green、Yellow、Grey、Magenta、Orange、Azure、Maroon。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:422:6. 新题的核心推理机制应明显不同——即从观察样例到归纳规则的认知路径不同，而不仅仅是场景、对象或颜色不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:423:7. 题目难度应来自机制的隐蔽性而非步骤数。用参考题作为难度标尺——如果你生成的题一个样例就能猜到规则，说明机制太透明，需要加深隐蔽性。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:424:8. 优先从参考题的机制出发进行重组或推演，而非从物理隐喻出发。物理隐喻容易导致大量题目归结为一种模式，例如\"沿方向移动到阻挡处停止\"。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:425:9. 题目的难度优先来自规则的**结构层数**，而不是单一步骤的复杂度。关于\"结构层数\"的判定标准：**只有解题者需要主动推理才能完成的步骤才算一层**。肉眼一扫即可获得的信息（如\"找到缺口在哪一侧\"、\"数出像素个数\"、\"识别哪个对象最大\"）不构成独立的推理层——它们只是变换的前置输入，不增加认知难度。真正的多层结构是指每一层都需要解题者发现一个非显然的规律。以两层结构为例：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:426:   - ✗ 伪两层：\"找到缺口方向\"→\"把东西推到对面\" — 第一步肉眼可见，实际只有一层推理。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:427:   - ✓ 真两层：\"通过孔洞数量匹配颜色图例\"→\"用匹配到的颜色重绘对象\" — 两步都需要非平凡的归纳。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:428:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:429:   如果你发现自己写出的题只是\"对每个对象，根据它的某个属性做某变换\"的单步规则，请引入一个需要主动推理的前置步骤。**用堆叠 tie-break 规则或复杂数学公式来\"加难度\"是劣解；用多一层需要归纳的结构嵌套来\"加难度\"才是好解**。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:430:10. 在符合ARC题目和提示词要求的基础上，鼓励尝试创新规则为多层结构的题目，不局限于两层，可以创新三层或四层结构的题目，但不可为了多结构层数违背要求。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:431:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:432:生成后对生成的题执行以下四项审查（审查内容不需要保存到文件）：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:433:1. 原创性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:434:  新题不可与上述参考题相同或类似，不可只是替换颜色、方向、对象类型等表层要素。判断标准：新题的核心推理路径应与任何一道参考题不同。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:435:2. 确定性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:436:  规则完全确定，同一输入只能产生唯一输出，每一步操作都有明确定义。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:437:3. 可实现性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:438:  所有必要细节都已给出——对象如何生成、如何识别、如何变换、边界情况如何处理，读完描述后可以直接写代码。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:439:4. ARC 合规性\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:440:  网格尺寸合理（≤30×30），使用颜色不超过 10 种，规则复杂度适中，人类能从 3-5 个样例中发现规律。没有使用上述注意事项第二条禁止使用的复杂计算。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1594776539/12/prompt.md:441:\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"实现方案定了：\n\n1. `main()` 会先按颜色找 4 连通组件，只接受“矩形边框减去一段 2 像素缺口”的组件作为容器。\n2. 对每个容器，读取其内部 grey 图案，识别缺口边，清空内部，再把图案按该边做镜像并反射到容器外，颜色改成边框色，越界则自然截断。\n3. `generate_input()` 会随机生成 2–4 个容器，均衡覆盖四个缺口方向；每个图案都从缺口后方生长，保证规则可见且不退化。\n4. 生成时会同时预留未来投射区域，避免不同容器在输出里互相打架；并保留一部分样例触发边界截断分支。"}}
